<title>ESTONIA: HOIU NOT TO CHANGE ITS STRATEGY.</title>
<headline>HOIU NOT TO CHANGE ITS STRATEGY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank said on Wednesday that a possible Swedbank purchase of the central bank's stake in its shares will not change its strategy.</p>
<p>&quot;Our present strategy has been correct and is not likely to change,&quot; deputy chairman Priit Haller told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The medium-term strategy of Hoiupank is to develop into an universal banking institution. </p>
<p>Hoiupank has not only focused its efforts on retail banking but has also participated actively in the corporate market and other financial services.</p>
<p>Hoiupank was the second largest Estonian bank at the end of May with total assets of 6.2 billion kroons.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
